      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(clickclack): wrap websocket message rejections with Error for diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe websocket message handler in ClickClack's gateway uses `.catch(reject)` to\nforward errors from the async message processor. When the processor throws a\nnon-Error value (a plain string, `undefined`, or a deserialized error from a\nremote system), the raw rejection loses the stack trace and makes downstream\nerror diagnostics unreliable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace `.catch(reject)` with an explicit catch block that preserves Error\ninstances and wraps non-Error values with context and the original value as\n`cause`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nTests pass:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm test extensions/clickclack/src/gateway.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  5 passed (5)\n```\n\nReal behavior proof — after-fix, all thrown value types produce diagnostic\nError instances; contrast with raw `.catch(reject)`:\n\n```text\n$ node proof-clickclack-rejection.mjs\nplain-string: instanceof Error=true hasCause=true message=plain-string\nnumber: instanceof Error=true hasCause=true message=number\nobject: instanceof Error=true hasCause=true message=object\nexisting-Error: instanceof Error=true hasCause=false message=real error\nraw .catch(reject): instanceof Error=false value=raw string\nPASS\n```\n\nThe http-client in the same extension already follows this pattern:\nall thrown errors are `new Error(...)` instances.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
        "branch": "sunlit/fix/clickclack-rejection",
        "head_sha": "3b072ee4a4358369e41179f89f3aadc2b91ceea9",
